        "v": 5,
        "title": "Align normal cost mode with max mode",
        "summary": "The 'normal' cost mode now mirrors 'max' mode behavior for agent operations, file requests, and deep thinking. Updates in `common/src/constants.ts` map 'normal' to `claudeModels.sonnet` for agent and file-requests, and `models.gpt4o` for check-new-files. Backend logic in `main-prompt.ts` and `gemini-with-fallbacks.ts` includes 'normal' in max-mode conditionals for `think_deeply` tool calls and Sonnet fallbacks. `request-files-prompt.ts` increases `countPerRequest` for 'normal' to 14 and enables non-obvious file prompts.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T14:59:56.314Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The assistant now uses the same, more capable model for routine tasks that it previously reserved only for the highest-power setting. When you ask it to work normally, it will now bring better reasoning and deeper thinking to agent operations, file look-ups, and follow-up checks than it did before. What you'll notice is that everyday requests get the more powerful treatment they were already giving to the top tier.",
