        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Improve Saxy text emission for split entities",
        "summary": "Saxy XML parser buffers text chunks and flushes at tag boundaries or stream end to handle split entities correctly. Added heuristic to only treat trailing ampersands as pending entities if followed by alphanumeric or hash characters. Updates `common/src/util/saxy.ts` to introduce `_textBuffer` and refine `parseEntities` position handling.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T14:57:20.132Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When software that reads XML files encounters a lone ampersand character (like the & in &amp;) at the very end of a chunk of text, it now checks whether that ampersand is actually the beginning of an entity (for example &copy;) by looking at the character that follows it. If the next character is a letter or a hash, the parser holds on to it, expecting the rest of the entity in the next chunk; otherwise, it treats the ampersand as ordinary text. This prevents the parser from incorrectly splitting up or misreading entities that happen to be cut off at the end of a text chunk, improving reliability when processing XML streams that arrive in pieces. The improvement is live and affects anyone receiving or parsing XML content in real time.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "04f3bf2d75df",
        "at": "2026-09-17T23:58:29.534Z"
      },
